---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import GuideSources from '../components/GuideSources.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Companies House identity verification: who, when and how"
  description="Companies House identity verification explained: who has to verify, the deadlines for directors and PSCs, verifying free with GOV.UK One Login or through an ACSP, and your personal code."
>
  <h1>Companies House identity verification</h1>
  <p>
    Since <Fact id="idv-mandatory-start" />, company directors and people with significant control (PSCs) have had to
    verify their identity with Companies House. Most people only do it once.
  </p>

  <h2>Who has to verify</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Company directors, and equivalents such as LLP members</li>
    <li>People with significant control (PSCs)</li>
    <li>Directors of overseas companies registered in the UK</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When you have to do it</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Who</th>
          <th scope="col">Deadline</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Existing directors</td>
          <td><Fact id="idv-existing-directors-deadline" /></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>New directors</td>
          <td><Fact id="idv-new-directors-deadline" /></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>People with significant control</td>
          <td><Fact id="idv-psc-deadline" /></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Two ways to verify</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Route</th>
          <th scope="col">Cost</th>
          <th scope="col">Good for</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>GOV.UK One Login</td>
          <td><Fact id="idv-route-one-login-cost" /></td>
          <td>Most people. Verify with the app, online, or by entering photo ID details and finishing at a participating Post Office.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>An Authorised Corporate Service Provider (ACSP)</td>
          <td><Fact id="idv-route-acsp" /></td>
          <td>People who can't use One Login or would rather use an agent. ACSPs can be based in any country.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Don't post or email identity documents to Companies House.</p>

  <h2>Your personal code</h2>
  <p>
    After you verify, you get a Companies House personal code. It belongs to you, not to a company. You give it when you
    file a confirmation statement, when you become a director, and when you become a PSC. Keep it as secure as your tax
    reference.
  </p>

  <h2>Starting a new company?</h2>
  <p>
    New directors give their personal code when the company is registered, so verify first. See
    <a href="/register-a-limited-company/">how to register a limited company</a>.
  </p>

  <GuideSources
    factIds={[
      'idv-mandatory-start',
      'idv-voluntary-start',
      'idv-existing-directors-deadline',
      'idv-new-directors-deadline',
      'idv-psc-deadline',
      'idv-route-one-login-cost',
      'idv-route-acsp',
    ]}
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
</style>
